Human: Can you tell me the steps to write an if/then statement in C programming language?

Assistant: Of course!  Here’s an example one-liner that demonstrates an if/then statement in C:

```
if (x > 10) {
    printf("x is greater than 10\n");
} else if (x == 10) {
    printf("x is equal to 10\n");
} else {
    printf("x is less than or equal to 10\n");
}
```

In this example we first check whether `x` is greater than 10.  If it is, we print the message “x is greater than 10”.  If it’s not, we move on to the next step, which is to check whether `x` is equal to 10.  If it is, we print the message “x is equal to 10”.  Finally, if neither of these conditions is true, we print the message “x is less than or equal to 10”.
